A||||9||RossT||Cool way to drain gas from tank.||||1||
Z||000000||RossT||11-12-2001||10:59 PM||||I used the "Dickman method"<P>disconnect left side of fuel filter (V-6), attach a hose to the fuel line, remove cigar lighter panel, jump pin G with the cigar lighter and way you go.  Drained about 6 gallons in 3-4 minutes.. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||11-12-2001||11:29 PM||||Good Method, Just be carefull doing that you don't run the pump dry.... You can fry the pump if you do. Chop the power as soon as fuel stops. That means if you are by yourself, put the catch bucket where you can see it and still reach the pump power quickly.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||RossT||11-12-2001||11:50 PM||||Also need to be careful that you only touch the inside of the cigar lighter assmebly.  If you jump it to the outside, you will short out the Cig. lighter and blow the BAT fuse.  I did it once.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||11-13-2001||01:25 PM||||Which pin is G?  Is it one of the diagnostic ones, or one of the other terminals sittin in there?||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||11-13-2001||01:49 PM||||the ALDL is in my cave and here...<A HREF="http://www.euronet.nl/users/fo_elmo/fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>Fiero-Tech-Zone</A> Make sure you know which way the key is pointing...<P>Don't touch the sides???? Just use an old power cord from a portable air pump or something. Or get a cheap cord at radio shack.... (Radar detector cords porbably aren't heavy enough...)<P>You could also cut the cover off a spare fuel pump relay and use it to switch on the pump. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||11-13-2001||02:10 PM||||If you have a fuel pressure gauge, you can remove the hose and extend it. Then connect the hose to the schrader valve in the fuel line. This way, you don't even have to get under the car.<P>You can also use the "Bat" terminal in the fuse block. (My lighter socket was bad.)<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000006||fieroparts.com||11-13-2001||02:47 PM||||Rosst<P>Why are you selling your low mile 88 GT?||||reg||14
Z||000007||rogergarrison||11-13-2001||02:50 PM||||more fun to just drive around till it quits.||||reg||1
Z||000008||ka4nkf||11-13-2001||07:25 PM||||This sounds good but the main reason I would want to drain my fuel tank would be to replace the bad fuel pump. So how do I drain it now.||||reg||1
Z||000009||mrfiero||11-13-2001||09:12 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ka4nkf:<BR><B>This sounds good but the main reason I would want to drain my fuel tank would be to replace the bad fuel pump. So how do I drain it now.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You don't!  There is no easy way to drain a tank without a running fuel pump.  <P>Removing a full tank is 1000 times easier than installing a full one!  Once the tank is removed then drain it through the top cam cover (where the fuel pump goes in).<P>I had the misfortune of removing a full tank from an '88 Formula......not fun.  What was even worse is I had nowhere to drain the gas, so I had to re-install a full tank as well.  My arms ached for a week!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  ||||reg||1
